WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.920
Los Angeles, 1906.

2
00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.700
In a former stable
building on Azusa Street,

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.510
a revival begins.

4
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.970
Its leader, William Seymour, is
an African American preacher.

5
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.960
Black and white worship together,
unusual in segregated America.

6
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.200
Within a few years, the
revival has spread to Europe,

7
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.310
Africa, Asia and Latin America.

8
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.410
New Pentecostal denominations form,
in the United States and in Britain.

9
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:34.060
So how did a small prayer meeting in Los
Angeles become a quarter of world Christianity?

10
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:39.380
In this mission, you'll trace the story
from Topeka to Azusa Street and beyond.

11
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.880
Then you'll meet its main beliefs, from
baptism in the Holy Spirit to the gifts

12
00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.900
of healing and prophecy.

13
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:50.760
Your mission: find out how this
movement spread so far, so quickly.
